WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.210
Domain 4 primer: Prompt Engineering & Structured Output.

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:11.764
Domain 4 is about getting output that is precise, consistent and machine-checkable, at scale and with honest gaps.

3
00:00:13.164 --> 00:00:17.315
Domain four treats a prompt as a specification for another system.

4
00:00:17.315 --> 00:00:26.373
When Claude's output feeds a parser, a database or a pull request, it has to be precise, consistent and structured, and someone has to check it.

5
00:00:26.373 --> 00:00:33.921
This domain is about a fifth of the exam and appears mostly in the continuous integration and data extraction scenarios.

6
00:00:35.321 --> 00:00:37.258
A few terms carry this domain.

7
00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:39.841
Explicit criteria spell out what counts.

8
00:00:39.841 --> 00:00:44.360
A false positive is a finding that turns out not to be a real problem.

9
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.911
Few shot means including worked examples in the prompt.

10
00:00:47.911 --> 00:00:52.754
A JSON schema, used through a tool and tool choice, fixes the output shape.

11
00:00:52.754 --> 00:00:57.273
And a batch sends many requests at once for later, cheaper processing.

12
00:00:58.673 --> 00:01:01.133
Picture a pipeline with four stations.

13
00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:04.951
First, instruct precisely with clear criteria and examples.

14
00:01:04.951 --> 00:01:09.158
Second, constrain the shape with a schema so parsing never fails.

15
00:01:09.158 --> 00:01:13.365
Third, verify the meaning in code and retry with specific errors.

16
00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:19.772
Fourth, scale up with batches where nobody is waiting, and double check with independent reviewers.

17
00:01:21.172 --> 00:01:23.821
The task statements map onto the pipeline.

18
00:01:23.821 --> 00:01:27.859
Four point one and four point two are about precise instruction.

19
00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:30.130
Four point three is about structure.

20
00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.157
Four point four is about validation and retries.

21
00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:39.465
Four point five and four point six are about running at scale and reviewing with independent passes.

22
00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.673
Each lesson zooms into one station.

23
00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:45.378
Here are the words this domain uses most.

24
00:01:45.378 --> 00:01:48.471
Pause the video and read through them, then keep going.

25
00:01:49.871 --> 00:01:51.853
Four ideas anchor domain four.

26
00:01:51.853 --> 00:01:54.497
Be specific, with criteria and examples.

27
00:01:54.497 --> 00:01:58.000
Use schemas for shape, but check the values yourself.

28
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.230
Retry with the exact error, and stop when the data is not there.

29
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:07.385
Batch work nobody waits for, and let an independent instance do the reviewing.

